================================================================================
SCOPE
================================================================================

The MIT License above covers the contents of this directory: the package
manifests under `plugins/`, `libraries/`, `presets/` and `packs/`.

It does not cover the rest of the repository. Luthier itself — everything
outside `bench/` — is licensed LGPL-2.1-or-later; see the `LICENSE` file at
the repository root. The split is deliberate: the tool stays copyleft, the
data stays maximally reusable, as it is in homebrew-core, nixpkgs and
winget-pkgs.

Two clarifications, because a registry describes things it does not own:

1. `schemas/package-v1.json` at the repository root is generated from the
   source of Luthier and carries documentation text taken from it. The
   copyright holder also makes that generated file available under the MIT
   License above, so that it may be redistributed alongside this data and used
   for editor completion without further conditions.

2. The software described by these manifests is licensed by its own authors,
   under their own terms. Nothing here relicenses any of it. Each manifest
   records the licence its upstream project states, in the `[license]` table,
   and that record is a statement of fact rather than a grant. Downloading and
   installing a package means accepting that project's licence, not this one.
